1. **Area of a Rectangle**: The area \( A \) of a rectangle can be calculated using the formula:
   \[
   A = \text{length} \times \text{width}
   \]
2. **Dimensions of the Outer Rectangle**: The dimensions of the outer rectangle (the red paper) can be determined by adding twice the width of the border to the dimensions of the picture.

