     \]
   - The height of the outer rectangle is:
     \[
     \text{Outer Height} = 7 + 2 \times 0.5 = 7 + 1 = 8 \text{ inches}
     \]

3. **Calculate the area of the outer rectangle**:
   - Using the area formula for rectangles:
   \[
   A_{\text{outer}} = \text{Outer Width} \times \text{Outer Height} = 6 \times 8 = 48 \text{ square inches}
   \]

