### 6. Significance of the Result
This result shows how the product of the proper divisors of a number can be systematically expressed in terms of its total number of divisors, illustrating the relationship between the structure of a number and its divisors. Understanding this relationship is fundamental in number theory and has implications in various mathematical fields, including combinatorics and algebra.
