This result shows how the parameters \( C \) and \( D \) influence the trigonometric functions of the angles \( A \) and \( B \). The simplification reveals a relationship between the constants and the sine and cosine of the sum of the angles, which can be useful in various applications, including physics and engineering, where angles and their relationships are critical.
