\]

### Significance of the Result
The direction vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\) indicates that the line \(\ell\) is oriented equally in all three coordinate directions, which is consistent with the symmetry of the reflection matrix provided. This result can be useful in applications involving geometric transformations and computer graphics.
