### 5. Significance of the Result
The result \( A - B = 8 \) indicates the difference between the sum of invertible and non-invertible integers modulo \( 16 \). This difference can provide insights into the structure of the integers under modular arithmetic, particularly in understanding how many integers are invertible compared to those that are not, which is crucial in number theory and cryptography.
