\]
Now substituting \( y \) back into the expression for \( z \):
\[
z = 6 - x - (29 - 2x) = 6 - x - 29 + 2x = x - 23
\]
Thus, we can express the line \( L \) in parametric form:
\[
\begin{align*}
x &= t, \\
y &= 29 - 2t, \\
z &= t - 23.
\end{align*}
