\]
The cross product is given by:
\[
\mathbf{n} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -28 \\ 24 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{vmatrix}
\mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
1 & -2 & 1 \\
1 & -28 & 24
\end{vmatrix}.
\]
Calculating the determinant:
\[
\mathbf{n} = \mathbf{i}((-2)(24) - (1)(-28)) - \mathbf{j}((1)(24) - (1)(1)) + \mathbf{k}((1)(-28) - (-2)(1)).
\]
This simplifies to:
\[
\mathbf{n} = \mathbf{i}(-48 + 28) - \mathbf{j}(24 - 1) + \mathbf{k}(-28 + 2) = \mathbf{i}(-20) - \mathbf{j}(23) + \mathbf{k}(-26).
