     Valid \(b\): \(0, 3, 6, 9\) (4 values)

   - **For \(a = 4\)**:
     \[
     2(4) + b \equiv 0 \pmod{3} \implies 8 + b \equiv 0 \pmod{3} \implies b \equiv 1 \pmod{3}
     \]
     Valid \(b\): \(1, 4, 7\) (3 values)

   - **For \(a = 5\)**:
     \[
     2(5) + b \equiv 0 \pmod{3} \implies 10 + b \equiv 0 \pmod{3} \implies b \equiv 2 \pmod{3}
