   \]

2. **Prime Factorization of 28**: 
   \[
   28 = 2^2 \times 7
   \]
   This means that any integer \( n \) that shares a factor of 2 or 7 with 28 will not be relatively prime to 28.

3. **Check Each Integer**: We will check each integer in the range \( 11 \) to \( 29 \) to see if it is relatively prime to 28 by calculating \( \text{gcd}(n, 28) \).

