The result \( 2 \) indicates that the expression \( \left(2^n\right)^2 - 2 \) simplifies to \( 2 \) when \( n \) is the modular inverse of \( 2 \) modulo \( 17 \). This showcases the relationship between modular arithmetic and exponentiation, which is fundamental in number theory and cryptography.
