### Step 2: Understanding the Concepts
The modular inverse \( a^{-1} \) of \( a \) modulo \( n \) exists if and only if \( a \) and \( n \) are coprime, i.e., \( \gcd(a, n) = 1 \). The equation \( a^{-1} \equiv a \pmod{24} \) can be rewritten as:
\[
